%% W2D6 — Supervisor vs. Swarm Networks — Request Lifecycle Sequence
%% Shows: task decomposition, parallel specialist dispatch, timeout handling,
%%        result aggregation, and partial-result fallback path.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Sup as Supervisor Agent
    participant Store as State Store
    participant Bus as Message Bus
    participant SA as Specialist A
    participant SB as Specialist B
    participant Agg as Aggregator

    User->>Sup: Submit request
    Sup->>Store: Persist initial task state
    Sup->>Sup: Decompose into subtasks A and B
    Sup->>Bus: Dispatch subtask A (idempotency key: k1)
    Sup->>Bus: Dispatch subtask B (idempotency key: k2)

    Note over Bus,SB: Independent subtasks execute in parallel

    Bus->>SA: Deliver subtask A
    Bus->>SB: Deliver subtask B

    SA->>SA: Execute task A
    SA-->>Agg: Return result A

    alt Specialist B completes within timeout
        SB->>SB: Execute task B
        SB-->>Agg: Return result B
        Agg->>Agg: Merge result A + result B
        Agg-->>Sup: Full aggregated result
    else Specialist B times out
        Note over SB: Timeout exceeded (e.g. 5s)
        Sup->>Sup: Apply fallback policy for subtask B
        Agg->>Agg: Merge result A + partial fallback for B
        Agg-->>Sup: Partial result with warning flag
    end

    Sup->>Store: Update task state to complete
    Sup-->>User: Final response (full or partial)
